==English==

===Etymology 1===
{{etyl|und|en}}; compare {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term|bindele||a binding”, “a tying|lang=ang}}.<ref name="OED1">“[http://dictionary.oed.com/cgi/entry/50022232 ˈbindle¹]” listed in the '''Oxford English Dictionary''' [2<sup>nd</sup> Ed.; 1989]</ref>

====Noun====
{{en-noun|?}}

# {{context|now|_|Scots}}<ref name="OED1"/> Any given [[length]] of [[cord]], [[rope]], [[twine]], etc, used to [[bind]] something.<ref name="OED1"/>

===Etymology 2===
Probably a corruption of {{term|bundle|lang=en}}; perhaps influenced by {{term|sc=Latinx|bindle#Etymology 1|bindle¹}}.<ref name="OED2">“[http://dictionary.oed.com/cgi/entry/50022233 bindle²]” listed in the '''Oxford English Dictionary''' [2<sup>nd</sup> Ed.; 1989]</ref>

